{"id":243,"date":"2020-10-02T17:21:59","date_gmt":"2020-10-02T16:21:59","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/?p=243"},"modified":"2020-12-23T15:01:13","modified_gmt":"2020-12-23T15:01:13","slug":"generic-data-source-for-parameters","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/2020\/10\/02\/generic-data-source-for-parameters\/","title":{"rendered":"Generic Data Source for Parameters"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I tend to use a lot of parameter actions to act as selections\/toggle in my dashboards, and have been thinking about how to make them easy to work with.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The two ways I have used in the past to create a toggle\/selection is to:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><li>Use data already in your data source to create the toggle if it exists, or create calculated fields to make the data<\/li><li>Create a small separate data source with the data in it.<\/li><\/ol>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I have found number two to be my favourite, and it works well when your toggle is not directly related to your data. However I have found using this method a bit of a pain when I need to keep updating the data source to add extra toggle functions, or items to a selection, as you need to re load the data in.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">So instead I have started using a &#8216;Generic&#8217; data source for my parameter actions which I can load in once, and then make any changes I need within Tableau. The data source looks like this:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"197\" height=\"341\" data-attachment-id=\"251\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-6\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image.png?fit=197%2C341&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"197,341\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image.png?fit=197%2C341&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image.png?resize=197%2C341&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-251\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I will use this in conjunction with another simple data set, in order to show the example, this data set looks like this:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"166\" height=\"248\" data-attachment-id=\"252\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-1-2\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-1.png?fit=166%2C248&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"166,248\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-1\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-1.png?fit=166%2C248&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-1.png?resize=166%2C248&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-252\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I want to simply have a colour toggle which changes how a chart looks, so I get something that does this:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"654\" height=\"447\" data-attachment-id=\"255\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/redbluetoggle-1\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/redbluetoggle-1.gif?fit=654%2C447&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"654,447\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"redbluetoggle-1\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/redbluetoggle-1.gif?fit=654%2C447&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/redbluetoggle-1.gif?resize=654%2C447&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-255\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">First I want to set up my colour selector as a separate sheet, using the generic parameter data source. I set up a parameter called pColour which will control the colour change:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"558\" height=\"284\" data-attachment-id=\"263\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-6-2\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-6.png?fit=558%2C284&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"558,284\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-6\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-6.png?fit=558%2C284&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-6.png?resize=558%2C284&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-263\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">And then I start setting up some calculations in my generic data set (note I converted my data to be a string dimension, rather than integer). The first one is &#8216;ParameterName&#8217; which I use to filter on the parameter I am interested in (or filter out nulls):<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"242\" data-attachment-id=\"256\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-2-2\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-2.png?fit=921%2C326&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"921,326\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-2\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-2.png?fit=685%2C242&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-2.png?resize=685%2C242&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-256\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">At the moment I only have one parameter, so I will label the first two elements of data as &#8216;pColour&#8217;. Then I will create a &#8216;SpecificName&#8217; field which will contain the actual data I want to select &#8211; in this case Red and Blue:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"242\" data-attachment-id=\"257\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-3-2\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-3.png?fit=920%2C325&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"920,325\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-3\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-3.png?fit=685%2C242&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-3.png?resize=685%2C242&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-257\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">With these set up I can then set up my selector sheet:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"324\" data-attachment-id=\"267\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-8\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-8.png?fit=914%2C432&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"914,432\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-8\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-8.png?fit=685%2C324&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-8.png?resize=685%2C324&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-267\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Note the ParameterName: pColour filter &#8211; this means it excludes any nulls, and also any other parameters we may add in future. Also note the &#8216;True&#8217; field and &#8216;False&#8217; filter &#8211; these are used in the dashboard which you will see later.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This then gets put on a dashboard along with a simple chart based off the actual data source:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"645\" height=\"512\" data-attachment-id=\"268\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-9\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-9.png?fit=645%2C512&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"645,512\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-9\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-9.png?fit=645%2C512&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-9.png?resize=645%2C512&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-268\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I then add a parameter action based off the selector sheet that updates the pColour parameter, this passes the &#8216;SpecificName&#8217; field to the parameter:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"502\" height=\"532\" data-attachment-id=\"272\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-11\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-11.png?fit=502%2C532&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"502,532\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-11\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-11.png?fit=502%2C532&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-11.png?resize=502%2C532&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-272\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This will update the parameter, but won&#8217;t do anything else yet as we need to add a field to the actual data source which will update based on the parameter, which I can then use to change the chart colour:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"235\" data-attachment-id=\"273\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-12\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-12.png?fit=906%2C311&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"906,311\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-12\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-12.png?fit=685%2C235&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-12.png?resize=685%2C235&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-273\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This field simply goes onto the colour shelf of the main chart, which you can then recolour based on what has been chosen. Now the parameter action works:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"654\" height=\"447\" data-attachment-id=\"255\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/redbluetoggle-1\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/redbluetoggle-1.gif?fit=654%2C447&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"654,447\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"redbluetoggle-1\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/redbluetoggle-1.gif?fit=654%2C447&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/redbluetoggle-1.gif?resize=654%2C447&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-255\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Note<\/strong>: This also uses a filter action trick to deselect the selector when the user selects it (as we don&#8217;t need it to remain selected). This action looks like the below:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"522\" height=\"689\" data-attachment-id=\"281\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-16\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-16.png?fit=522%2C689&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"522,689\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-16\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-16.png?fit=522%2C689&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-16.png?resize=522%2C689&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-281\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This is a neat trick that essentially passes a &#8216;True&#8217; field through to the same sheet you selected from, but with the Target as &#8216;False&#8217;. This essentially filters everything off the view, but by choosing &#8216;Show all values&#8217; on selection clear, this puts the view all back in again.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This might seem a long winded way of doing it, but now it is set up it is very easy to add extra colours, or even extra selectors. To add an additional colour I just need to add a couple of lines to the following fields, and update the main chart colour:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"241\" data-attachment-id=\"259\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-4-2\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-4.png?fit=917%2C322&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"917,322\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-4\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-4.png?fit=685%2C241&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-4.png?resize=685%2C241&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-259\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"240\" data-attachment-id=\"260\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-5-2\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-5.png?fit=916%2C321&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"916,321\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-5\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-5.png?fit=685%2C240&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-5.png?resize=685%2C240&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-260\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To give the below:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"654\" height=\"447\" data-attachment-id=\"262\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/redbluetoggle2\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/redbluetoggle2.gif?fit=654%2C447&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"654,447\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"redbluetoggle2\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/redbluetoggle2.gif?fit=654%2C447&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/redbluetoggle2.gif?resize=654%2C447&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-262\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">And to add a different selector, I can add additional rows to the same fields, but this time changing the parameter name. For this example I am using an Asc\/Desc option:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"235\" data-attachment-id=\"278\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-14\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-14.png?fit=905%2C310&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"905,310\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-14\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-14.png?fit=685%2C235&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-14.png?resize=685%2C235&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-278\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"234\" data-attachment-id=\"279\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-15\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-15.png?fit=904%2C309&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"904,309\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-15\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-15.png?fit=685%2C234&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-15.png?resize=685%2C234&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-279\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Then I can set up another selector sheet, filtering the ParameterName on &#8216;pAscDesc&#8217; and create the selector as before. This will update a parameter called &#8216;pAscDesc&#8217;.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I also want a new field in the main data source that I can sort on, based on this parameter:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"234\" data-attachment-id=\"283\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/image-17\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-17.png?fit=903%2C308&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"903,308\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"image-17\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-17.png?fit=685%2C234&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/image-17.png?resize=685%2C234&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-283\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This just reverses the value based on the Asc\/Desc flag. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This can be added to the dashboard in the same way as the colour selector and you now have a two selector dashboard, with the selectors both running off the generic data source:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"654\" height=\"553\" data-attachment-id=\"286\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/redblueordertoggle-1\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/redblueordertoggle-1.gif?fit=654%2C553&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"654,553\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"redblueordertoggle-1\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/redblueordertoggle-1.gif?fit=654%2C553&amp;ssl=1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/redblueordertoggle-1.gif?resize=654%2C553&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-286\" \/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The only additional thing I did with the change order selector, is to add a flag to the generic data source to highlight if the parameter is selected or not, so I could get the grey and blue colouring.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The Tableau Public viz is here:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https:\/\/public.tableau.com\/views\/TogglewithGenericParameters\/GenericParameterToggle\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:\/\/public.tableau.com\/views\/TogglewithGenericParameters\/GenericParameterToggle<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Thanks! <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Ant.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Using a generic data source to power a number of different toggles on a dashboard, allowing the ability to quickly add and remove elements as required without reloading data.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":191258845,"featured_media":291,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_coblocks_attr":"","_coblocks_dimensions":"","_coblocks_responsive_height":"","_coblocks_accordion_ie_support":"","advanced_seo_description":"","jetpack_seo_html_title":"","jetpack_seo_noindex":false,"jetpack_seo_schema_type":"","_jetpack_newsletter_access":"","_jetpack_dont_email_post_to_subs":false,"_jetpack_newsletter_tier_id":0,"_jetpack_memberships_contains_paywalled_content":false,"_wpcom_ai_launchpad_first_post":false,"_jetpack_feature_clip_id":0,"_jetpack_memberships_contains_paid_content":false,"footnotes":"","jetpack_publicize_message":"","jetpack_publicize_feature_enabled":true,"jetpack_social_post_already_shared":false,"jetpack_social_options":{"image_generator_settings":{"template":"highway","default_image_id":0,"font":"","enabled":false},"version":2},"jetpack_post_was_ever_published":false},"categories":[2708],"tags":[678609322,852300],"class_list":["post-243","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-how-to","tag-parameter-action","tag-tableau"],"jetpack_publicize_connections":[],"jetpack_featured_media_url":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/10\/redblueordertoggle-2.gif?fit=654%2C553&ssl=1","jetpack_likes_enabled":true,"jetpack_sharing_enabled":true,"jetpack_shortlink":"https:\/\/wp.me\/pchcDm-3V","jetpack-related-posts":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/243","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/191258845"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/consult-ant.uk\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=243"}],"version-history":[{"count":25,"href":